Optional Kalman filter for the position of a DFT pen in contact (InkFilter)

A filter with position and a decaying velocity as state, the same on both axes. A measurement
is trusted less when the phases of the three antennas around the tip disagree (which they do
when something other than the tip tone contributes: noise, the barrel of a tilted pen), and the
model follows faster when the pen is fast. The time between samples is taken from the window
timestamps. When the contact ends, the distance between the filtered and the measured position
is faded out over 5 samples.

This is the kind of filter Windows runs on the pen position. Measured by replaying captures of
handwriting from the Surface Pro 9: the roughness of the path (distance of a sample from the
cubic through its four neighbours, moving pen) goes from 0.011 .. 0.027 mm to 0.005 .. 0.012 mm
(median), and from 0.041 to 0.014 mm for a pen held at 37 degrees, at the price of the reported
position trailing the pen by 0.16 .. 0.24 mm (median, 4 .. 6 ms). With it the reported position
is within 0.05 .. 0.07 mm (median) of what Windows reports for the same frames, without it within
0.17 .. 0.22 mm, nearly all of which is that lag. Off by default.

